<h1>Lesson 3: Design Foundations</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lessons 3-5</div>

<p>This lesson prepares you to teach three curriculum lessons:</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 3:</b> Intro to CSS</p>
<a href="[LESSON 3 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 3</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 4:</b> Accessibility in Design</p>
<a href="[LESSON 4 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 4</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 5:</b> Wireframes</p>
<a href="[LESSON 5 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 5</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this lesson, you'll:</b></p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Read a CSS rule and watch it change a live page in real time</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Practice prompting like a developer using Goals, Constraints, and Edge Cases</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Learn wireframes and the POUR accessibility principles</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Spot real accessibility barriers on a mock site and match them to POUR</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• Try a Web Lab practice activity yourself</p>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #222222; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
<p><b>💡 Notice as you explore:</b> how styling decisions and accessibility are the same conversation, not two separate topics, and how AI reproduces accessibility gaps from its training data unless someone specifically checks for them.</p>
</div>

<hr>

